  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the following two planes:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x-2z+13=0 \\\\ 2y-3z-25=0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $5x-2z+13=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=\u27e85,0,-2\u27e9.$\n\n- For the plane $2y-3z-25=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=\u27e80,2,-3\u27e9.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =\u27e85,0,-2\u27e9\\times \u27e80,2,-3\u27e9 \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 5 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =4i+15j+10k \\\\  & =\u27e84,15,10\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
